  <abstract format="text/plain" language="en" script="Latn">Telecommunication devices and equipment can use non-linear limiting, linear attenuating, or both types of functions to mitigate surges occurring on services. Isolating transformers attenuate common-mode voltage surges on a service. Recommendation ITU-T K.95 gives test methods and preferred values for the isolating transformer surge parameters that are harmonized with established international standards on insulation coordination levels and test techniques.</abstract>
